{
  "case_id": "2019-19-161",
  "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:07 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Department of Homeland Security",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress established the expedited removal system in 1996 for aliens who arrive at our borders or enter illegally and have no entry documents. Such aliens are clearly inadmissible and have no right to be in this country."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent contends that the Suspension Clause requires a fact-laden judicial review of the negative fear -- credible-fear determination made in that screening process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Kneedler, it's one thing when an alien comes and has no protected ground to stay here. There's no legal right to stay. And so expedited proceedings are okay because they have no right to be here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: -- your view, you know, does not only speak to pure factual matters. Your view applies to legal matters and mixed questions as well."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, there's a view as to whether the hearing officer filed the -- followed the appropriate procedures."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Counsel GELERNT",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And we think Congress's judgment that that is not constitutionally required is entitled to great respect."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0001-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are 9,000 -- as we point out in our brief, there are 9,000 negative credible-fear determinations that have been made in recent years, 100,000 credible -- credible-fear referrals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But wasn't it true in the -- in the finality era cases that the individuals, once it was determined that they had not been properly detained, they did have a right to be in the United States, because, in those -- in that era --for most of that era, or much of that era, there were not very many restrictions on immigration to the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "the government was very clear that the Suspension Clause requires some review, that the finality era statutes limited review to the constitutional requirement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What are the concrete issues that could be raised on habeas in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There have been as our count 9500 people who failed their CFI and who could have filed a habeas under our rule. Only 30 have."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF EDWIN S. KNEEDLER ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONERS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Shouldn't the Court count for something? Hasn't it been under"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: We have the great writ. It was there to ensure that the executive acts according to law. What's left if you tell me that there are laws, but there's no judicial review of whether those laws are being followed or not? That's my question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-19-161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c6b9ff3eec57b16f8bdf81f7023b292fda599ae83bce0e4745432cdda1ad89a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c6b9ff3eec5-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
